-- title:
--   Publish n scalar bits in order into the native address bank.
-- statement:
--   Publish n scalar bits in order into the native address bank. On return both
--   address cursors point just after their words. Only address registers 0–2 and
--   the destination window, and scalar registers 3,4,5,8, are written. The scalar
--   source can be anywhere disjoint from those four scratch cells.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.publishDenominator_spec`, `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.publishNumerator_spec`.
